#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/struct.md:43
msgid "The diagram can now be expanded as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/struct.md:45
msgid ""
"```bob\n"
"                                                     +------+\n"
"                                             finish  |      |\n"
"                          serialize          struct  V      |\n"
"                          struct\n"
"+--------------------+ --------------> +-------------------------+\n"
"| \"Serializer<Root>\" |                 | \"Serializer<Struct<S>>\" |\n"
"+--------------------+ <-------------- +-------------------------+\n"
"                         finish struct\n"
"         |                                     serialize   |\n"
"         |                                     property    V\n"
"         |\n"
"finish   |                           +-----------------------------------+\n"
"         V                           | \"Serializer<Property<Struct<S>>>\" "
"|\n"
"                                     +-----------------------------------+\n"
"     +--------+\n"
"     | String |\n"
"     +--------+\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/struct.md:67
msgid "A `Struct` can only contain a `Property`;"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/struct.md:69
msgid ""
"Finishing a `Struct` returns control back to its parent, which in our "
"previous slide was assumed the `Root`, but in reality however it can be also "
"something else such as `Struct` in case of nested \"structs\"."
msgstr ""
